    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Luis wants to make a pattern by colouring the sides of the triangles shown in the diagram. He wants each triangle to have one red side, one green side and one blue side. Luis has already coloured some of the sides as shown. What colour can he use for the side marked $x$?",
    "image": "qimages/ukmt/grey-2015/q15.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "only green"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "only blue"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "only red"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "either blue or red"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "The task is impossible"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Force the colours",
        "body": "Every triangle needs one side of each colour. In each end triangle two sides are given (blue and green), so the third side is red. Working along the strip, each next triangle already has one forced side and one given side, which forces its third side. The side $x$ lies in a triangle that already has a blue and a red side, so $x$ must be green.\n\n**Answer: (A) only green**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "logic"
    ],
