    "prompt": "Ria wants to write a number in each of the seven bounded regions in the diagram. Two regions are neighbours if they share part of their boundary. The number in each region is to be the sum of the numbers in all of its neighbours. Ria has already written in two of the numbers, as shown. What number must she write in the central region?",
    "image": "qimages/ukmt/grey-2015/q17.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "0"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$-2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$-4$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "6"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Add the equations",
        "body": "The four regions that neighbour the $-4$ region have numbers $a,b,c,d$, and their sum is $-4$ (the number in the $-4$ region). The region marked $2$ has exactly the same four neighbours plus the central region, so $a+b+c+d+\\,?=2$. Hence $-4+\\,?=2$, so $?=6$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 6**"
      }
    ],
