    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Five points lie on a straight line. Alex finds the distances between every pair of points. He obtains, in increasing order, 2, 5, 6, 8, 9, $k$, 15, 17, 20 and 22. What is the value of $k$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "14"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "13"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "12"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "11"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "10"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use the largest distances",
        "body": "The five points $P,Q,R,S,T$ in order with $PT=22$ the largest distance. The next largest, 20, is $PS$ or $QT$; take $QT=20$, so $PQ=2$. The next largest is 17: it cannot involve $PR$ or $RT$ combinations giving 3, so $PS=17$ and $ST=5$. Then $QS=15$. The remaining distances $6,8,9,k$ are $PR,QR,RS,RT$ with $QR+RS=15$, so $\\{QR,RS\\}=\\{6,9\\}$. Then $PR=2+6=8$ (taking $QR=6$) and $RT=22-8=14$. So $k=14$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 14**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
