    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Gregor divides 2015 successively by 1, 2, 3, and so on up to and including 1000. He writes down the remainder for each division. What is the largest remainder he writes down?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "55"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "215"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "671"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "1007"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "some other value"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Aim for the form 2d+(d-1)",
        "body": "The remainder on dividing by $d$ is at most $d-1$. For $d\\le 671$ this is at most 670. For larger $d$ up to 1000 the quotient is at least 2; with quotient 2 we get remainder $2015-2d$, which is largest for the smallest such $d$. Quotient 2 works when $2d+(d-1)\\ge2015$, i.e. $d\\ge 672$, and $d=672$ gives remainder $2015-1344=671$. For $d>672$ the remainder $2015-2d<671$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 671**"
      }
    ],
